\par
     NOTE TO THE PUBLIC\par
\par
     The Hon. Lyman J. Gage, Dr. Funk and hundreds of others have said\par
     that my book should be put at a price which would place it within\par
     the reach of every young man, etc.\par
\par
     Hitherto, it has been sold by subscription at $3.50, $5 and $10 per\par
     copy--the five editions printed having been easily sold at those\par
     prices.\par
\par
     Notwithstanding the thousands of friends their circulation has\par
     made, I did not care to have my family name go any further in this\par
     connection than financial needs required in working for the release\par
     of the men still undergoing life sentences in English prisons.\par
\par
     At last, however, certain influence causes me to let it go in the\par
     revised and improved form here presented, and may it prove as\par
     valuable and engrossing to the general public as it has to 20,000\par
     subscribers to former editions. GEORGE BIDWELL.\par
